have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/45/450bbc1c472dd6a5f2189bbc1954beb04aa29a2520947ec1a4e3c14a6133103c.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$." 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761363 1072 #uuid "179bf212-0bfb-539a-ad37-65e12d98e79f" 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761363 1074 "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, ending at $A$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &=1\\,(0, -5)=(0, -5). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{AC} &=(10, 0).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/c5/c51cfbbc29a6d168dbc17af3246d3a21ff7d9933884d0fe244e2823f6501f555.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(4, 0)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{10}{4}=\\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{AC}=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{5}{2}$." 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761364 1080 "3" 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761364 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761364 1083 #uuid "1efb5c11-7107-5152-b142-4077afc16f07" 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761365 1080 "2" 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761365 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761365 1083 #uuid "1ffcfe9a-be2d-5fc7-89a2-c62865b13541" 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761366 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761406 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761366 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761366 1071 "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/ca/ca3040f396ac5cfeccb90e25fbad3267b749fb578ba4f255e6bdbbd567fbfa99.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$." 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761366 1072 #uuid "28970578-230e-5966-8ec4-d81dc2c75265" 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761366 1074 "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, ending at $B$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &=1\\,(0, 3)=(0, 3). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{BC} &=(12, 0).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/7b/7b4b470475e9fe60956e13f41b8d20f10c0cee78d3993492d66c9436dec834ec.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(4, 0)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{12}{4}=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{BC}=3\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OB}+\\overrightarrow{BC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{b}+3\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=3$." 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761367 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761367 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761367 1083 #uuid "2a4e045a-bebb-57ef-85b0-3d7713f9e677" 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761368 1080 "2" 13194139547588 17592186576411 true] [17592186761368 1082 #edb/ref